{
  "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
  "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
  "model": "Z1000 HVAC drive (embedded BACnet MS/TP)",
  "model_slug": "z1000",
  "aliases": [
    "Z1000",
    "CIMR-ZU",
    "CIMR-ZUA",
    "Z1000 AC Drive for HVAC Fan and Pump",
    "SIEP C710616 45"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive (HVAC)",
  "applies_to": "Yaskawa Z1000 HVAC fan and pump drives (CIMR-ZU, 200 V and 400 V class) using the built-in RS-485 port with H5-08 set to BACnet.",
  "summary": "The Z1000 has BACnet MS/TP built into its RS-485 terminals; set H5-08 = 3 to select it. The fixed object list covers analog and digital I/O, run/fault/reset commands, the frequency and PI setpoint references, output monitors and a long set of fault and status flags. AV29/AV30 give indirect access to any drive parameter by Modbus register number.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "PICS lists application software 1.3, firmware VSE90101X",
  "default_device_instance": 1,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object IDs marked Not used (AI3-AI5, AV24) are left out. AV15-AV17 (MF Input Status, Drive Status 2, MF Output Status) are named in the table but have no register, units or access, so they are left out too.",
    "AV1, AV4 and AV5 are packed command words; the manual says not to use them together with the single-bit objects they duplicate (AV1 with BV1-BV11 or AV5, AV4 with BO1-BO3 or BV12, AV5 with AV1, BO4 or BV9-BV11).",
    "Frequency units follow the o1-03 display setting.",
    "AV29/AV30 with BV55/BV56 read and write drive parameters that are not in the object list.",
    "The device object name is writable from BACnet (20 characters) and takes effect after a power cycle.",
    "Each description gives the drive's Modbus register where the manual lists one."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "YASKAWA AC Drive Z1000, AC Drive for HVAC Fan and Pump, Programming Manual (Appendix B, BACnet Communications)",
    "doc_number": "SIEP C710616 45F",
    "revision_date": "2021-06",
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=SIEPC71061645&cmd=documents&documentName=SIEPC71061645.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set H5-08 = 3 (BACnet), the MS/TP address in H5-01, the baud rate in H5-02 and the device instance in H5-14/H5-15, then cycle power. Set b1-01 = 2 and b1-02 = 2 so the network supplies the frequency reference and run command. Write BV1 RUN FWD and AV2 Frequency Command, read BV13/BV16 and AV10/AV12/AV13, and reset faults with BV4.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "RUN FWD",
        "why": "Start/stop from the BMS (drive)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "Frequency Command",
        "why": "Frequency reference, units per o1-03"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 4",
        "name": "FAULT RESET",
        "why": "Reset a tripped drive"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 13",
        "name": "RUN-STOP",
        "why": "Running status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 15",
        "name": "READY",
        "why": "Drive ready to run"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 10",
        "name": "Output Frequency",
        "why": "Output frequency, units per o1-03"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 12",
        "name": "Output Current",
        "why": "Motor amps"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 13",
        "name": "Output Power",
        "why": "Drive power in kW"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 16",
        "name": "FAULT",
        "why": "Any active drive fault"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 7",
        "name": "Fault Details (Bitmapped)",
        "why": "Bit-coded active fault flags"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Table B.1: set b1-01 Frequency Reference Selection 1 = 2 and b1-02 Run Command Selection 1 = 2 (serial communication); b1-15/b1-16 = 2 do the same for External Reference 2. With H5-12 = 0 (default) BV1 runs forward and BV2 runs reverse; with H5-12 = 1 bit 0 is run/stop and bit 1 sets direction. Monitoring, parameter access, fault set/reset and the multi-function inputs work at any time, whatever b1-01/b1-02 are set to.",
    "heartbeat": "H5-05 = 1 (default) turns on CE detection: if the drive gets no data from the master for H5-09 (0.0-10.0 s, default 2.0 s) it raises a CE fault and acts per H5-04 (0 ramp to stop, 1 coast, 2 fast stop, 3 alarm only and keep running (default), 4 run at d1-04).",
    "remote_sensors": "AV3 PI Setpoint lets the BMS write the PI setpoint; BO4 Ref Sel: PI Setpoint (or AV5 bit 1) selects it. The object list has no writable PI feedback.",
    "setup": [
      "H5-08 = 3 selects BACnet; H5-01 is the MS/TP address (0-FFH, default 1FH) and must be unique.",
      "H5-02 sets the baud rate, 1200 to 76800 bps (BACnet default is setting 3 = 9600 bps); 115200 bps gives an oPE29 error.",
      "H5-03 sets parity (default none); data is 8 bits with 1 stop bit.",
      "Device instance = H5-14 (low word) + H5-15 (high word), in hex; default 1. Example: 1234 is H5-14 = 4D2H, H5-15 = 0.",
      "H5 settings and the device instance take effect after a power cycle.",
      "Up to 127 drives per MS/TP segment."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "H5-04 defaults to Alarm Only, so the drive keeps running when BACnet traffic stops.",
      "BV56 Parameter Enter writes EEPROM (rated about 100,000 writes); don't use it cyclically.",
      "Don't mix the packed words (AV1, AV4, AV5) with the single-bit BV/BO objects they duplicate.",
      "Terminal inputs and BACnet multi-function inputs are ORed together.",
      "Frequency objects use the o1-03 display units, which are not always Hz."
    ]
  },
